    delphi:hasVerdict "resolvable-now" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.84"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The geometric and abundance predictions are direct and large public datasets provide broad coverage. Standard occupancy models can account for effort, allowing a decisive present-day test across many species pairs." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Estimate range widths and overlap-zone widths for geographically replacing close relatives, and fit abundance changes toward each boundary. Overlap zones consistently narrow relative to each range and abrupt edge declines support the claim; broad overlap or gradual transitions refute it." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Occurrence density reflects observer effort as well as abundance.", "Hybrid zones and patchy habitat complicate a single overlap-width measure." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch06-02--gpt--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch06-02--gpt--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch06-02--gpt--dataset-3> .
